<title>AUSTRALIA: Australia Feb private sector credit rose 0.4 pct.</title>
<headline>Australia Feb private sector credit rose 0.4 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank of Australia (RBA) said private sector credit extended by financial intermediaries rose by 0.4 percent in February, seasonally-adjusted, after rising 1.0 percent in January.</p>
<p>For the year to February, credit rose by 10.1 percent.  </p>
<p>The RBA detailed the change in financial aggregates as follows, seasonally-adjusted in percentage terms --</p>
<p>				     Feb 97	Jan 97  Feb 96/Feb 97</p>
<p>    Total credit		 +0.4	  +1.0	  +10.1</p>
<p>    M3			     +1.2	  +0.8	   +9.2</p>
<p>    Broad money		  +1.1	  +0.7	   +9.8</p>
<p>-- Private Sector Credit</p>
<p>    Housing			+1.0	  +0.9	  +10.3</p>
<p>    Business			0.0	  +1.0	   +9.6</p>
<p>    Other Personal use	 +0.7	  +1.0	  +11.6</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
